When sorting by titles, there is an issue if the title starts with spaces. So when creating/copying/editing, we have to trim the package title and should trim existing packages/courses and purchased packages titles.

To avoid this issue, I have added a temporary fix; it will take unnecessary performance. After we add a fix for titles, we can remove this.
```
//TODO: need to trim package title when creating/copy/edit packages and courses, and should trim existing titles of purchase packages/ courses / packages.
{
    $addFields: {
       packageTitle: {
          $trim: {
             input: { $ifNull: ['$title', ''] },
          },
       },
    },
},


if (Object.keys(sort).includes('title')) {
   const [sortValue] = Object.values(sort);
     sort = {
       packageTitle: sortValue,
      };
  }
```

We are currently saving actualDuration and agreedDuration as string values. It will not give a good way to store number values in the database, because of which we can't sort duration easily. So we have to convert those two values to int.

<img width="516" height="135" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2cc1184a-f335-4cd9-87e9-e2b33005d859" />

I have currently added a fix for sorting to `getTeamCoachingLogs()`. So after we change the above-mentioned type of the fields, we can remove that type conversion because it's an additional step.

``
//TODO: we are saving actual duration as string, we need to change it to number otherwise sort will not work as expected
                    actualDurationNumber: {
                        $toInt: '$actualDuration',
                    },
``

